.TH FL-EDIT 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.0" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-edit \- text editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-edit\fR [\fIFILE\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A tabbed text editor with find and replace (Ctrl+F, Ctrl+H, F3), go to line (Ctrl+G), auto-indent,
block indent with Tab/Shift+Tab, word wrap and line numbers.
.SS Syntax highlighting
The language is detected from the file name or the first line (\fB#!\fR interpreter,
\fB<?php\fR, \fB<!DOCTYPE html>\fR, \fBdiff\fR headers). Supported: C/C++, C#, CMake, CSS, Diff, Go,
HTML (with embedded JavaScript and CSS), INI, Java, JavaScript, JSON, Kotlin, Lua, Makefile, Markdown,
Meson, Perl, PHP, Python, Ruby, Rust, Shell, SQL, TOML, TypeScript, XML and YAML.
\fBView \(-> Language\fR overrides the detection for the current tab.
.PP
\fBView \(-> Color Theme\fR picks the highlighting colors: Automatic (follows the desktop's light or
dark theme), Default Light, Default Dark, Solarized Light, Solarized Dark, Monokai or High Contrast.
\fBView \(-> Highlight Matching Brackets\fR marks the bracket next to the cursor and its partner;
brackets inside strings and comments are ignored.
.SS Language servers
When a language server for the file's language is installed, fl-edit starts it and talks to it
(the Language Server Protocol): problems are underlined (red for errors, blue for warnings), counted
in the status bar with the message for the current line, and marked in the minimap. F8 and
Shift+F8 go to the next and previous problem, Ctrl+Space completes the word at the cursor and F12
goes to the definition of the name at the cursor. One server runs per project folder (the nearest
folder up with \fB.git\fR, \fBcompile_commands.json\fR, \fBCargo.toml\fR, \fBgo.mod\fR,
\fBpackage.json\fR, \fBpyproject.toml\fR and the like). The servers used: \fBclangd\fR (C/C++),
\fBpylsp\fR (Python), \fBrust-analyzer\fR, \fBgopls\fR, \fBtypescript-language-server\fR
(JavaScript, TypeScript), \fBbash-language-server\fR, \fBlua-language-server\fR and others;
\fB[LanguageServers]\fR in the settings file chooses another, e.g.
\fBpython=pyright-langserver --stdio\fR. \fBCode \(-> Language Servers\fR turns them off.
.SS Multiple carets
Ctrl+D selects the word at the cursor, then adds the next place with the same text as another
selection. Alt+click adds a caret (Ctrl+Alt+click when Alt+drag moves windows), Ctrl+Alt+Up and Ctrl+Alt+Down add one on the line above or
below. Typing, Backspace, Delete, Enter and the arrow keys then work at every caret; Escape (or
a click) goes back to one.
.SS Minimap and session
\fBView \(-> Minimap\fR shows the whole document beside the text, with the visible part shaded;
click or drag in it to scroll. The open files, their cursors and scroll positions are saved at
quit and opened again when fl-edit starts without files (\fBOptions \(-> Reopen Files at
Start\fR).
.PP
\fBView > Check Spelling\fR (F7) underlines misspelt words: everything in plain
text, the text of Markdown, and comments and strings in code. A right-click on
one offers suggestions, adds it to the personal dictionary or ignores it. The
languages are set in Settings > Language & Region (enchant with Hunspell
dictionaries).
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.config/fldesktop/edit.ini\fR
Settings: \fBColorTheme\fR, \fBMatchBrackets\fR, \fBHighlight\fR, \fBFontSize\fR, \fBTabWidth\fR,
\fBMinimap\fR, \fBLanguageServers\fR, \fBRestoreSession\fR and others; \fB[LanguageServers]\fR
\fIlanguage-id\fR=\fIcommand\fR.
.TP
\fI~/.config/fldesktop/edit-session.ini\fR
The files open at the last quit.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfl-wm\fR(1), \fBfl-session\fR(1), \fBfl-panel\fR(1)
